From 1c1992297527ef4b58a3ca4ed6f96241c0711493 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 12:23:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(hooks): defer the D20 auto-heal when the index is
 partially staged
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The hook decided WHETHER to regenerate from the staged paths but regenerated by
reading the live working tree, so under partial staging (`git add -p`, or a file
staged then edited again) it committed an artifact describing content that is not
in the commit — a generated file lying about its own source.

Reading staged blobs instead would mean re-implementing the census against
`git cat-file` while auditBdCallSites() walks the filesystem, recreating the
predicate/census divergence this branch just fixed. So the hook now checks whether
any counted staged path also has unstaged changes (`git diff --name-only -z` over
exactly those paths, NUL-parsed, untrimmed) and defers when one does: it prints an
actionable notice to stderr, exits 0 so the commit is not blocked, and leaves
`forge release regen-audit` plus the d20-audit-artifact-current gate as the path
to a correct artifact.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
